w("## 2. What the product actually is (read from the code)\n")
w("- Python **standard library only** backend (`http.server`), 5 simulated clients x 5 sentences each (25 records), a **character-bigram language model** (33-symbol alphabet, 33x33 = 1,089 parameters) standing in for an LLM adapter update. No PyTorch / Flower / Hugging Face model is used; it is a demonstrator.")
w("- Training: each client's bigram-count vector is L2-clipped (C = 25), summed, Gaussian noise N(0, (sigma*C)^2) is added per coordinate (sigma = 3), and the result is divided by the client count. All 5 raw update norms (25.22-28.23) exceed C, so all 5 are clipped (scale 0.886-0.991).")
w("- Unlearning: the stored clipped update of the chosen client is subtracted from the noisy aggregate and the sum is divided by (n-1). The same stored noise vector is kept.")
w("- Certification: re-computes the retained-only aggregate from the stored updates **and the same noise** and takes the L2 distance; status CERTIFIED if distance <= 1e-10 and utility retention >= 70 %. Because both sides use identical stored values, the check is exact by construction (algebraic identity), not an independent retrain.")
w("- Epsilon: epsilon = sqrt(2 ln(1.25/delta)) / sigma, delta = 1e-5 -> **epsilon = %.4f**. This is the classical one-shot Gaussian-mechanism bound, which is only valid for epsilon < 1 (needs sigma > %.3f); the default sigma = 3 is outside that range." % (F.dp["default_epsilon"], F.dp["sigma_needed_for_epsilon_below_1"]))
w("- Membership inference: loss-based attack AUC of the client's 5 records vs 5 fixed non-member sentences (AUC resolution 0.04).")
w("- Audit: append-only JSONL, each record SHA-256 over previous hash + canonical JSON; `verify()` re-walks the chain.")
w("- Utility score = 0.65 * next-char accuracy + 0.35 / (1 + ln(1 + perplexity)); retention = after/before x 100 (capped at 100).\n")

